  "stdout": "reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Sodium_Glutamate_Monohydrate.after.yaml:2:preferred_term: Sodium glutamate monohydrate\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Sodium_Glutamate_Monohydrate.after.yaml:5:  ontology_label: monosodium L-glutamate hydrate\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Sodium_Glutamate_Monohydrate.after.yaml:14:    notes: molecular_formula 'C5H8NO4.Na' -> 'C5H8NO4.H2O.Na'. The recorded value described the anhydrous salt while the label names a hydrate, understating the mass by 18 g/mol per water. Corrected because adopted verbatim from the mapped term CHEBI:232425 ('monosodium L-glutamate hydrate'), which is the specific hydrate and already carries the water.\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Sodium_Glutamate_Monohydrate.after.yaml:16:    source: all_unmatched_20261107 worker04 primary proposal glutamate-monohydrate\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Sodium_Glutamate_Monohydrate.after.yaml:17:    notes: NBRC1625 explicitly specifies L-glutamic acid monosodium salt monohydrate. CHEBI:232425 has one water and L stereochemistry, so the existing monohydrate owner is the correct identity. Its InChI/SMILES still omit water despite the correct formula; repair those exact form properties and add the explicit L alias. Ingredient1291 explicitly names sodium glutamate monohydrate and supplies CAS6106-04-3 and mass187.13, consistent with monosodium L-glutamate monohydrate232425. Its older anhydrous CHEBI annotation is not controlling. The owner has the correct formula but dehydrated InChI/SMILES; the shared exact-form repair is appropriate while all publication holds remain. Evidence and exact frozen scope are recorded in reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/fragments/chemistry-decisions.json. This proposed delta does not approve complete owner/export payload or remove inherited holds.\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Sodium_Glutamate_Monohydrate.after.yaml:28:- synonym_text: Glutamate Sodium\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Sodium_Glutamate_Monohydrate.after.yaml:31:- synonym_text: Glutamate monosodium salt\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Sodium_Glutamate_Monohydrate.after.yaml:40:- synonym_text: L(+) Sodium glutamate\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Sodium_Glutamate_Monohydrate.after.yaml:49:- synonym_text: Natrium L-hydrogenglutamat\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Sodium_Glutamate_Monohydrate.after.yaml:55:- synonym_text: Sodium hydrogen glutamate\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Sodium_Glutamate_Monohydrate.after.yaml:78:  changes: Added CAS-RN:6106-04-3 from PubChem API via name lookup (Sodium glutamate monohydrate)\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Sodium_Glutamate_Monohydrate.after.yaml:103:  changes: 'ontology_label ''Sodium glutamate monohydrate'' -> ''monosodium L-glutamate'': synced to canonical CHEBI label (preferred_term ''Sodium glutamate monohydrate'' unchanged).'\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Sodium_Glutamate_Monohydrate.after.yaml:111:  changes: 'Re-grounded CHEBI:64243 ''monosodium L-glutamate'' -> CHEBI:232425 ''monosodium L-glutamate hydrate'' (EXACT_MATCH). The record is the monohydrate: its cas_rn 6106-04-3 was set by an independent PubChem name lookup on ''Sodium glutamate monohydrate'', and CHEBI:232425 ''monosodium L-glutamate hydrate'' (formula C5H8NO4.H2O.Na) is the matching term. It was on CHEBI:64243 (anhydrous, ChEBI CAS xref 142-47-2) only because the specific term was never found. Monohydrate 187.13 vs anhydrous 169.11 g/mol is a 10.6% weigh-out difference across the 11 media using it.'\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Sodium_Glutamate_Monohydrate.after.yaml:118:  changes: molecular_formula 'C5H8NO4.Na' -> 'C5H8NO4.H2O.Na' (#321); adopted verbatim from the mapped term CHEBI:232425 ('monosodium L-glutamate hydrate'), which is the specific hydrate and already carries the water.\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Sodium_Glutamate_Monohydrate.after.yaml:127:  changes: 'Recovered 1 surface form(s) that the published SSSOM `other` carried but no curated record did, so a rebuild would have dropped them from KGX: ''Glutamate Sodium''. Tokens already present on the kg-microbe ontology node were left out as redundant (#520).'\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Sodium_Glutamate_Monohydrate.after.yaml:132:  changes: 'Recovered 10 surface form(s) that the published SSSOM `other` carried but no curated record did, so a rebuild would have dropped them from KGX: ''Glutamate monosodium salt''; ''Glutamic acid, monosodium salt''; ''Glutammato monosodico''; ''L(+) Sodium glutamate''; ''MSG''; ''Monosodioglutammato''; ''Natrium L-hydrogenglutamat''; ''Natriumglutaminat''; ''Sodium hydrogen glutamate''; ''sodium (2S)-2-ammoniopentanedioate''. Tokens already present on the kg-microbe ontology node were left out as redundant (#520).'\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Sodium_Glutamate_Monohydrate.after.yaml:137:  changes: 'Isolated source-review proposal glutamate-monohydrate: added aliases [''L-glutamic acid monosodium salt monohydrate'']; rejected provenance labels []. Corrected hydrate InChI/SMILES to include one water. Subject to independent skeptical review and guarded coordinator integration; inherited full-payload support must not transfer.'\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Na_Glutamate.after.yaml:2:preferred_term: Na glutamate\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Na_Glutamate.after.yaml:5:  ontology_label: monosodium glutamate\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Na_Glutamate.after.yaml:13:    source: all_unmatched_20261107 worker04 primary proposal monosodium-glutamate-alias\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Na_Glutamate.after.yaml:14:    notes: Ingredient839's Na glutamate is concordant with one-sodium glutamate64220 and mass169.112; it does not specify L or a hydrate. The existing owner has that identity but still carries an active wrong Na2-glutamate alias; its monohydrate alias is already REJECTED_LABEL. The matching source is scientifically distinguishable from those conflicts, and publication remains held pending owner cleanup. Ingredient415's Na2-glutamate implies two sodium ions but its automatic CAS142-47-2, CHEBI64220 and169.111mass describe one sodium. The current monosodium owner wrongly exports the disodium string; stoichiometric disagreement must be fixed in the source or separated, not silently normalized. Evidence and exact frozen scope are recorded in reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/fragments/chemistry-decisions.json. This proposed delta does not approve complete owner/export payload or remove inherited holds.\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Na_Glutamate.after.yaml:16:- synonym_text: Na2-glutamate\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Na_Glutamate.after.yaml:25:- synonym_text: Sodium glutamate\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Na_Glutamate.after.yaml:28:- synonym_text: Monosodium glutamate\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Na_Glutamate.after.yaml:49:- synonym_text: Sodium glutamate·H2O\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Na_Glutamate.after.yaml:66:  changes: Added CAS-RN:142-47-2 from PubChem API via name lookup (Monosodium glutamate)\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Na_Glutamate.after.yaml:72:  changes: Added CAS-RN:142-47-2 from PubChem API (ontology label) via name preprocessing (Monosodium Glutamate)\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/pro